    <string name="progress_scoring_title">How scoring works</string>
    <string name="progress_scoring_shown">Explanation shown</string>
    <string name="progress_scoring_hidden">Explanation hidden</string>
    <string name="progress_scoring_answers">Each answer counts once, right or wrong.</string>
    <string name="progress_scoring_chords">Each answer counts once, right or wrong. Questions about chord quality and about inversion are counted separately; choose which above.</string>
    <string name="progress_scoring_progressions">Each chord after the opening tonic counts on its own, so one wrong chord costs one point rather than the whole progression. Each session also shows how many progressions were fully right.</string>
    <string name="progress_scoring_dictation">Each note after the opening tonic counts on its own, so one wrong note costs one point rather than the whole melody. Each session also shows how many melodies were fully right.</string>
    <string name="progress_scoring_rhythm">Each rhythm figure counts on its own, on the beat where it was played, so one wrong figure costs one point rather than the whole rhythm. Each session also shows how many rhythms were fully right.</string>
